🔟 What is Invalid Certificate Exception?
Invalid Certificate Exception occurs when the browser encounters a security certificate that is not valid or trusted. This can happen if the certificate has expired, is self-signed, or is issued by an untrusted authority. In Selenium, you can handle this exception by configuring the browser to ignore certificate errors.
ChromeOptions options = new ChromeOptions();
options.setAcceptInsecureCerts(true); // Accepts insecure SSL
options.addArguments("--ignore-certificate-errors");

