❓ Can we override a constructor in Java?

❌ No, we cannot override a constructor in Java.

🔍 Why Not?
Constructors are not inherited, and overriding only applies to inherited methods.

Since constructors are class-specific and not part of the object's polymorphic behavior, you can't override them in a subclass.

